The preceding reflections also suggest statements such as the following: For a given locally noetherian base scheme $S$, the functor $X\longrightarrow X_{\mathrm{et}}$, going from the category \deleted{reduced} of\inserted{ reduced} schemes locally of finite presentation over $S$, to the 2-category of \unsure{topoi} over $X_{\mathrm{et}}$, is \deleted{fully} 1-faithful (two homomorphisms $f,g:X\unsure{=|\rightrightarrows}Y$ such that the homomorphisms\inserted{ $f_{\mathrm{et}},g_{\mathrm{et}}$} of topoi $X_{\mathrm{et}}\rightrightarrows Y_{\mathrm{et}}$ over $S_{\mathrm{et}}$ are \unsure{equal|$fg$} isomorphic, are equal) and $\unsure{=|\overline m}$ perhaps \uline{fully} \uline{faithful}, when one passes to the category of fractions of $(\mathrm{Sch}_{\unsure{l.t.f.}})/S$ obtained by making the universal homeomorphisms invertible\ldots Experiment with \deleted{\unsure{p}} this for example for the automorphisms of a proper algebraic curve over a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, by \inserted{re}discovering the ``fact'' that every outer automorphism of $E_K$ ($K$ the function field of $X$) which respects the \unsure{loop|Qcts} structure and which commutes with the action of $\Gamma$, comes from an automorphism of $X$
